# Example 05: a prediction colored by its own confidence.
# AlphaFold DB model for SpCas9, UniProt Q99ZW2. pLDDT rides in the
# B-factor column, so the alphafold palette reads it directly.
#
# Rule: this coloring judges a model. It does not make a structural claim.
# A figure that argues about mechanism should not be colored by confidence;
# put confidence in its own panel, as BindCraft does.
alphafold fetch Q99ZW2
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

color bfactor #1 palette alphafold

view
view pad 0.05

key alphafold :0 :50 :70 :90 :100 pos 0.04,0.3 size 0.03,0.4 fontSize 17 labelSide right/bottom
2dlabels text "pLDDT" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.74 size 18 color lab_black bold true
2dlabels text "AlphaFold DB  Q99ZW2" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.04 size 18 color lab_gray

save alphafold_plddt.png width 1800 supersample 3
